§ `Q9 -- son bit claimant's ankle; wellness proof provided 6 months after the effective date; claimant was serving as a police officer at the time`

-- Judgement call: the cause of the hospitalization (a child biting his parent's
-- ankle) does not arise out of police service, even though the claimant happened
-- to be serving as a police officer at the time. Section 2.1(4) excludes events
-- that arise "directly or indirectly out of" service in the police, not every
-- event that happens to a person who is a police officer. See NOTES.md.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`                        IS TRUE
    `age at hospitalization`                                                      IS 35
    `hospitalization arose out of skydiving`                                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization arose out of military service`                               IS FALSE
    `hospitalization arose out of fire fighter service`                           IS FALSE
    `hospitalization arose out of police service`                                 IS FALSE
    `committed fraud misrepresentation or material withholding`                   IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date that the wellness visit occurred`           IS JUST 1
    `months after the effective date that wellness visit confirmation was given` IS JUST 6
    `months after the effective date of the hospitalization`                     IS 6

#EVAL covered q9
